<figure class="exhibit" data-exhibit="wakeword" data-src="/data/wakeword-clips.json" id="fig-01">
  <div class="exhibit__bar">
    <span class="mono"><strong>Fig. 01</strong> · wake-word detector · “Go Gators”</span>
    <span class="ticks" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="mono" data-mode-label>mode: precomputed</span>
  </div>

  <div class="ww-clips" role="group" aria-label="Demo clip" data-clips>
    <noscript><p class="mono">Interactive exhibit requires JavaScript.</p></noscript>
  </div>

  <button class="btn ww-record" type="button" data-record
    title="Records 3 seconds from your microphone and scores it with the trained network locally in your browser. Nothing is uploaded.">
    <span class="ww-record__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    Record 3 s · say “Go Gators”
  </button>

  <p class="mono" data-status hidden aria-live="polite" style="margin: 0.4rem 0"></p>

  <canvas data-spec height="160" role="img" aria-label="Mel spectrogram of the selected audio"></canvas>
  <canvas data-gauge height="56" role="img"
    aria-label="Wake-word detection score against the 0.5 threshold"
    style="margin-top: 0.6rem"></canvas>

  <label class="mono" for="ww-scrub" data-scrub-label style="display:block; margin-top:0.6rem">Scrub</label>
  <input type="range" id="ww-scrub" data-scrub min="0" max="300" value="0" step="1" />

  <div class="ctl-row">
    <button class="btn btn--red" type="button" data-play aria-pressed="false">Play ▸</button>
    <p class="readout">
      <span data-ro-time>t = 0.00 s</span>
      <span data-ro-score>p = –</span>
      <span data-ro-state aria-live="polite">listening…</span>
    </p>
  </div>

  <figcaption class="figcap mono">
    Real recordings, real inference: an encoder trained on Google Speech Commands
    with a classifier head, fine tuned on “Go Gators”, scores each 3 s window.
    Sigmoid output above the red 0.5 threshold = wake word. That threshold can be
    tuned depending on whether you prioritize false positives or false negatives.
    “Record 3 s” scores your own attempt with the exported ONNX network locally in
    your browser. Audio never leaves your device.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

